                        X server test suite

This suite contains a set of tests to verify the behaviour of functions used
internally to the server.

= How it works =
Through some automake abuse, we link the test programs with the same static
libraries as the Xorg binary. The test suites can then call various functions
and verify their behaviour - without the need to start the server or connect
clients.

This testing only works for functions that do not rely on a particular state
of the X server. Unless the test suite replicates the expected state, which
may be difficult.

= How to run the tests =
Run "make check" in the test directory. This will compile the tests and execute
them in the order specified in the TESTS variable in test/Makefile.am.

Each set of tests related to a subsystem are available as a binary that can be
executed directly. For example, run "xkb" to perform some xkb-related tests.

== Adding a new test ==
When adding a new test, ensure that you add a short description of what the
test does and what the expected outcome is.

== Acceleration pixel baseline ==

Run `meson test -C build accel-pixels` for the Xvfb framebuffer reference.
The test compares every pixel after a clipped CopyArea, a software write
followed by another copy, and an ARGB icon composited with an A8 mask onto
a pixmap and a manually redirected window. Failures report the operation,
pixel coordinates and expected and actual values.

On a running depth-24 Fission session, run `build/test/accel-pixels` with
DISPLAY and XAUTHORITY set for that session. Keep the same GPU, driver,
depth, compositor and scale when comparing AccelMethod "vaccum" and
"glamor". The client redirects its own window and reads back its backing
pixmap. For scanout checks, run pattern-present separately and record
Present completion modes, including whether each frame copied or flipped.

== VACCUM pixmap backing ==

Run `build/test/vaccum-pixmap` on a depth-24 VACCUM screen. It checks
reproducible sequences of CPU writes, CopyArea, GetImage, destruction,
and DRI3 sharing. The test compares pixels with a CPU reference and
verifies dma-buf row padding after writes through an imported alias.
It also verifies a long chain of dependent copies on large pixmaps while
freeing the last source before the destination readback. It compares
clipped copies and DRI3 round trips at depths 16, 24, 30, and 32 when
the server exposes those formats.

== Explicit Present synchronization ==

Run `build/test/present-syncobj` on a DRI3-capable VACCUM display at depth
24. The test uses two X clients and reuses a pixmap across delayed acquire
points above 32 bits. It checks that the observer remains responsive, that
the window shows the previous pixels before acquire, and that rewriting
the mapped dma-buf immediately after release preserves the presented
pixels. It also checks release for a superseded Present, a destroyed
window, and
producer disconnect when another client owns the target window.

Run with `--flip` on an uncomposited Fission VACCUM screen that allows
fullscreen flipping. This checks delayed acquire, retirement after a
replacement flip, and release after destroying the fullscreen window or
disconnecting its producer.
Use `--flip-fallback` with flipping disabled to check the copy path when
a fullscreen client does not request PresentOptionCopy.

Run with `--unavailable` on a VACCUM display without DRM timeline support
to check version negotiation, Present capabilities and rejected imports.
